      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">IO Zoom VPS Review 2026: KVM from $10/mo, 8 DCs</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-base">Last updated: August 22, 2026 · 10 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-5">

      <p>IO Zoom is a budget <strong>KVM VPS</strong> provider that competes on an unusual combination: a genuinely global <strong>8-datacenter footprint</strong> across the US and Europe, <strong>true KVM virtualization with full root access</strong> on every plan, and <strong>10 Gbps DDoS protection included as standard</strong> — all from a <strong>$10/month unmanaged entry point</strong>. We pulled the live pricing and specs from iozoom.com (HTTP 200, fully-rendered pricing page) to verify exactly what you get, and where the value case for developers holds up.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">IO Zoom at a Glance</h2>
      <p>IO Zoom positions itself as a developer-friendly budget host: virtualized KVM with no artificial restrictions, full root access, open-source Linux distributions only, and free migrations from other providers. Its headline is the network — <strong>10 Gbps DDoS protection on every tier</strong>, a feature most budget hosts reserve for higher plans or gate behind add-ons.</p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-300">
        <li><strong>Niche:</strong> Budget KVM VPS with a global US/EU datacenter footprint and 10 Gbps DDoS standard</li>
        <li><strong>Virtualization:</strong> True KVM with full root access on all plans</li>
        <li><strong>Network:</strong> 10 Gbps DDoS protection included; unmetered bandwidth with fair-use limits (2–12 TB)</li>
        <li><strong>Datacenters:</strong> 8 locations (US: Atlanta, Chicago, Dallas, Los Angeles, Miami, New Jersey; EU: Frankfurt)</li>
        <li><strong>OS options:</strong> CentOS, Fedora, Ubuntu, Debian (all open source)</li>
        <li><strong>Management:</strong> Unmanaged from $10/mo; managed with cPanel from $20/mo</li>
        <li><strong>Entry plan:</strong> KVM 2GB at $10/mo unmanaged — 2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM, 20 GB SSD, 2 TB bandwidth</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Pricing Table (Verified 2026-08-22)</h2>
      <p>All prices below were pulled from <a href="https://www.iozoom.com/linux-vps/" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">iozoom.com/linux-vps</a> on August 22, 2026 (HTTP 200, ~1 MB fully-rendered page). Plans are billed monthly; the managed tier adds cPanel to the same base specs.</p>

